# Entry 3: Adding Stabilizers and Hardware Anchors

After reviewing the official Hack Club KEEB Docs layout guide I realised I needed to add hardware stabilizers right on the schematic layer. 

I thenwent back to the sheet, pressed 'A', and pulled in 4 'MX_stab' mechanical components to support my wider keys .
I put them next to my matrix block and ran the schematic annotation tool to assign them unique designators (S1 through S4). While updating this,
I also mapped out my 6 protective M3 tray-mount chassis mounting holes (H1 to H6) to make sure the board structurally mounts to an enclosure later without bending.
The entire core blueprint done
